      "writtenOn": "2022-07-21T16:42:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In upstream Zephyr, how will users set 1.8V support for a pin that isn\u0027t a GPIO?  Zephyr upstream doesn\u0027t include the \u0027named-gpios\u0027 node, so there doesn\u0027t appear to be any place where users can configure an I2C bus for 1.8V operation.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 231,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 231,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "82d767553201efa402eec3173ea09833415ada2f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6fca11bb_f45c206a",
        "filename": "zephyr/projects/herobrine/gpio.dts",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 231,
      "author": {
        "id": 1121210
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-25T07:43:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it depends on how the application layer configures gpio pins via gpio api functions. On chromium ec, we use `named-gpios` DT node to configure pins in the [shimmed driver](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/refs/heads/main/zephyr/shim/src/gpio.c#285). On Zephyr upstream repo, there are no strict rules between gpio api functions and DT nodes. The basic principle is that users need to add a DT node with `phandle-array` property for GPIO module cells at the board DT file. Then, use GPIO DT macros to get necessary information used by gpio api such as `gpio_pin_configure_dt()`. \n\nHence, we might configure i2c port to 1.8V without `named-gpios` DT node by:\n1. Declare a DT nod with `phandle-array` property for GPIO module cells first.\n2. Add gpios which i2c port is 1.8V with GPIO_VOLTAGE_1P8 flag in this DT node. \n3. Use `gpio_pin_configure_dt` gpio api during initialization in application layer",
      "parentUuid": "7a82d855_0474accf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 231,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 231,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "82d767553201efa402eec3173ea09833415ada2f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
